<title>HONG KONG: Hung Hing interim net rises 47.8 percent.</title>
<headline>Hung Hing interim net rises 47.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   17.9	vs  12.1</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    4.0	 vs  4.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  1.10 gain vs  11.27 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    82.36     vs  55.74</p>
<p>    Turnover		     570.70    vs  542.51</p>
<p>    Company name		 Hung Hing Printing Group Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  December 27-31, 1996</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   January 28, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - Hung Hing manufactures packaging.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on write back of provision for diminution in value of listed investments.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
